; wwmi-dx12 LOD texture matches. One line per target:  <target> = <low> <flags> | <low> <flags> ...
; A low is a lower-resolution texture the game streams in; it is swapped as its target's mod texture.
;   mip=K         the low is the target's mip K (0: the level is not known)
;   exact=1       proven from the game's own data: the target's own mip, or a stream copy
;   exact=0       only looks alike (tex_look, its reference in tex_look.bin): with lod_resemblance=1 swapped like
;                 an exact low; under several targets, as the one ahead by 0.03 ssim, else not at all
;   chain=1       learned through a chain of stream copies; a look-alike learned so has the ssim of the one it came through
;   ssim=S        a look-alike's lowest patch similarity to the target's reference (1: identical)
;   place=1       a look-alike by where it is drawn: HD drew the target at that slot of a mod's component
; degenerate = <low> <low> ...  identical to the mips of more than one target: never swapped, never learned again
